WEBVTT

00:11.644 --> 00:16.144
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

00:16.983 --> 00:20.444
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

00:22.238 --> 00:26.738
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

00:27.410 --> 00:31.247
<i>But I will never give in</i>

00:31.289 --> 00:35.789
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

00:43.092 --> 00:47.592
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

00:56.147 --> 01:00.647
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

01:02.111 --> 01:06.611
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

01:09.201 --> 01:12.329
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

01:12.413 --> 01:16.913
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

01:17.626 --> 01:22.126
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

01:31.640 --> 01:36.019
EPISODE 20
THE FINAL MISSION FROM THE BOSS

01:38.481 --> 01:40.024
What's our estimated arrival?

01:41.025 --> 01:42.609
Well, we're almost at
the Rialto Bridge.

01:42.985 --> 01:44.569
So I'd say another five minutes.

01:44.653 --> 01:46.571
Good… Onward and upward then.

01:46.655 --> 01:50.033
Bucciarati, so what did
the boss have to say?

01:51.327 --> 01:54.371
I'm checking the boss's most recent
directive now.

01:55.998 --> 01:59.710
I TRUST THAT THIS MESSAGE
FINDS YOU IN SAFETY.
KNOW THAT YOU HAVE
MY ETERNAL GRATITUDE
FOR SAVING MY DAUGHTER, TRISH.

01:59.001 --> 01:59.731
Here's what he wrote.

02:00.503 --> 02:02.087
I inputted the information
onto this disc

02:02.171 --> 02:06.466
when you and your team boarded
the train in Napoli.

02:06.926 --> 02:10.471
I, therefore, have no means of
knowing at the present moment,

02:10.554 --> 02:13.181
the number of your pursuers,

02:13.224 --> 02:16.894
or the number of men
you have possibly lost.

02:17.561 --> 02:19.229
This disc will tell you everything
you need to know

02:19.271 --> 02:22.232
to safely rendezvous
with my daughter.

02:22.525 --> 02:24.235
It is your final mission.

02:24.318 --> 02:27.529
I must also tell you that
it is absolutely imperative

02:27.571 --> 02:32.071
that you follow my directions
in exactly the way I prescribe.

02:33.202 --> 02:34.703
If you or any of your men
take any action

02:34.745 --> 02:36.329
that deviates from my directive,

02:36.372 --> 02:39.249
regardless of whether
the act is accidental,

02:39.291 --> 02:43.086
I will be forced to consider it
a clear indication of mal-intent.

02:43.838 --> 02:45.548
Now for my directive.

02:48.217 --> 02:50.260
You are to travel to

02:51.053 --> 02:53.096
the island of San Giorgio Maggiore.

02:53.514 --> 02:55.474
There, with my daughter in tow,

02:55.558 --> 02:58.185
you shall climb to the top of
the basilica's campanile.

02:58.769 --> 03:00.896
Upon your safe delivery
of my daughter,

03:00.938 --> 03:02.773
you will have completed
the mission.

03:03.649 --> 03:06.610
Rule number one, because there
is no stairway to the top…

03:06.694 --> 03:10.114
and because only one elevator can
reach the peak of the bell tower…

03:10.739 --> 03:12.615
only Trish and
one accompanying protector

03:12.658 --> 03:14.368
shall board the elevator
to the top.

03:14.994 --> 03:16.078
Rule number two,

03:16.120 --> 03:18.455
the said protector must not be
in possession of any objects.

03:18.539 --> 03:21.750
That includes knives,
guns, and portable phones.

03:22.334 --> 03:25.503
Rule number three,
you must disembark within

03:25.588 --> 03:27.881
fifteen minutes of retrieving
this disc.

03:28.132 --> 03:30.843
The disc is equipped
with a transmitter,

03:30.926 --> 03:33.595
allowing me to follow
your movements.

03:34.180 --> 03:36.974
Rule number four, everyone else
must remain on the boat.

03:37.016 --> 03:38.434
Moving ashore
is strictly forbidden.

03:39.101 --> 03:40.143
That is all.

03:41.770 --> 03:43.813
Bucciarati, looks like we made it.

03:45.983 --> 03:49.069
So the boss is at the top
of that very tower…

03:49.570 --> 03:52.614
Well, he's certainly detailed,
not to mention extremely careful.

03:53.282 --> 03:57.077
Then again, I suppose he has to
as head boss of the organization.

03:57.203 --> 04:00.831
I can't believe this will be
the end of our mission.

04:00.915 --> 04:03.834
We're all alive.
What more can we ask for?

04:03.918 --> 04:07.004
We're alive, all right,
but barely.

04:07.296 --> 04:08.630
We made it to
the famous city of water.

04:08.672 --> 04:10.006
We should have a little fun.

04:10.090 --> 04:11.549
It's known for its cuisine too.

04:11.634 --> 04:13.385
They've got good chow here?

04:13.469 --> 04:16.305
Geez, I forgot how hungry I was.

04:16.347 --> 04:17.931
So what's the local specialties?

04:18.474 --> 04:19.892
Well, they've got
pasta al nero di sepia

04:19.975 --> 04:21.518
and insalata di granchio,

04:21.602 --> 04:25.897
and then, there's the carpaccio
at the Hotel Cipriani.

04:25.981 --> 04:27.023
Listen, children!

04:27.525 --> 04:29.151
Let me remind you!

04:29.276 --> 04:31.194
We are all still on assignment!

04:31.612 --> 04:33.655
Narancia, keep an eye
on the radar.

04:33.697 --> 04:34.864
S-Sure.

04:35.491 --> 04:36.533
Bucciarati,

04:37.034 --> 04:39.453
if I may, I offer myself up
as guardian.

04:39.912 --> 04:43.206
I'll accompany Trish up to
the top of the campanile.

04:43.958 --> 04:46.418
Well aren't you considerate!

04:46.502 --> 04:48.712
Is there some reason why you think
our capo, Bucciarati,

04:48.754 --> 04:50.464
shouldn't take Trish to the boss?!

04:50.756 --> 04:52.632
The only reason the boss
didn't designate someone

04:52.675 --> 04:54.677
is because he didn't know
who was still alive!

04:57.596 --> 04:59.806
Thank you, men, but I'll go.

05:00.599 --> 05:01.683
Come, Trish.

05:01.892 --> 05:04.769
As ordered, two people are about
to disembark this vessel.

05:14.321 --> 05:15.363
<i>This is it.</i>

05:15.698 --> 05:17.950
<i>This is our chance to learn
the boss's true identity</i>

05:18.075 --> 05:19.659
<i>We will make it happen.</i>

05:20.369 --> 05:21.578
Hey, Giorno,

05:21.704 --> 05:24.081
what do you think about
lending me a little luck

05:24.123 --> 05:25.916
on this last mission from the boss?

05:26.792 --> 05:28.752
Some call it the child of the sun.

05:29.253 --> 05:30.921
Some see them as symbols of life.

05:31.755 --> 05:33.423
It's like a talisman, yes?

05:34.174 --> 05:35.508
Oh, I guess so.

05:35.843 --> 05:38.929
Yes, ladybugs are
bringers of good luck.

05:43.726 --> 05:46.687
<i>This brooch is pulsating with life
thanks to Golden Wind.</i>

05:46.729 --> 05:49.106
<i>It will be our beacon.</i>

05:49.690 --> 05:50.691
Bucciarati.

05:51.525 --> 05:52.526
What, Fugo?

05:53.193 --> 05:55.653
I suppose this is the most
appropriate time to tell you…

05:56.238 --> 05:57.822
Why so formal all of a sudden?

05:58.699 --> 06:02.619
I knew you were destined
to become capo,

06:02.661 --> 06:05.872
and I know, standing here today,
you will carry out this mission.

06:06.957 --> 06:08.166
We all know that.

06:10.502 --> 06:13.713
Together, I know we can work
our way all the way to the top!

06:15.424 --> 06:17.300
Yeah… I suppose so.

06:17.843 --> 06:19.845
It's about time, Trish.

06:23.641 --> 06:27.519
<i>As long as I can affix this
to the boss,</i>

06:27.728 --> 06:30.063
<i>Giorno will be able to
track his every move.</i>

06:31.607 --> 06:33.942
<i>We will unveil
the boss's identity…</i>

06:34.610 --> 06:35.777
<i>We have to.</i>

07:28.789 --> 07:30.874
<i>He left the door open.</i>

07:32.334 --> 07:35.295
Only two buttons. The ground floor
and the top of the campanile.

07:35.462 --> 07:37.714
It's a direct shot,
no way to stop in between.

07:37.798 --> 07:38.799
What's…

07:40.092 --> 07:42.385
What's going to happen to me?

07:43.595 --> 07:46.472
First, I'm kidnapped by
a bunch of mafiosi,

07:46.515 --> 07:47.974
and am pushed
face to face with death,

07:48.684 --> 07:53.146
and now, I'm being delivered to
a father I've never even met…

07:53.939 --> 07:57.317
Where do I go from here?

07:59.862 --> 08:03.448
The boss's sole concern is
your complete and total safety.

08:04.241 --> 08:06.409
As for your immediate
and long-term future,

08:06.994 --> 08:08.954
I think I can offer some insight…

08:09.371 --> 08:11.373
First, you'll be given
a different name.

08:12.332 --> 08:14.709
You may need to surgically
alter your appearance.

08:14.752 --> 08:16.962
You will likely assume
a completely new identity.

08:17.588 --> 08:19.464
You will reside in
a locale unknown to us,

08:20.174 --> 08:21.758
somewhere far from
where we are now…

08:21.800 --> 08:23.009
but you will know happiness.

08:23.761 --> 08:24.970
I assure you your father has
the means and power

08:25.053 --> 08:27.055
to do all he can
to make that happen.

08:28.348 --> 08:30.433
Here, take my hand.

08:36.607 --> 08:37.774
You know…

08:38.567 --> 08:41.778
It's weird,
I'm not even nervous…

09:09.097 --> 09:10.139
I wonder…

09:10.808 --> 09:13.310
if I'll grow to love him.

09:15.312 --> 09:18.148
You do not need to worry
about any such thing.

09:21.443 --> 09:22.485
Yeah…

09:23.070 --> 09:24.321
You're right.

09:24.780 --> 09:28.617
I guess it is silly to worry
about stuff like that.

09:29.284 --> 09:31.411
We're here… This is it.

09:38.752 --> 09:40.462
Trish? Tri—

09:49.805 --> 09:52.516
W-What?!

09:53.684 --> 09:56.853
Trish… No… What's—?

09:58.021 --> 10:01.232
<i>We're the only ones
supposed to be here.</i>

10:01.650 --> 10:04.986
<i>The only people who know about this
are my team members and…</i>

10:05.445 --> 10:07.321
<i>No… There's no way!</i>

10:07.364 --> 10:08.823
<i>Could the boss…</i>

10:09.324 --> 10:11.826
<i>Was this all just a ploy
to maintain his anonymity…?</i>

10:12.160 --> 10:15.037
Did he assign the mission of
protecting his daughter…

10:15.372 --> 10:18.958
just so he could be sure
to eliminate her

10:19.001 --> 10:21.128
with his own evil hands?!

10:30.012 --> 10:33.432
<i>Bruno Bucciarati was born
the son of a fisherman</i>

10:33.515 --> 10:35.850
<i>in a small town outside Napoli</i>

10:36.226 --> 10:38.895
<i>Often labeled
reserved and stand of fish,</i>

10:38.937 --> 10:40.939
<i>Bruno's father lived
a life of purpose and integrity.</i>

10:41.148 --> 10:42.941
<i>More than anything,</i>

10:43.025 --> 10:45.402
<i>he fought to protect his family
from life's cruelties.</i>

10:47.446 --> 10:48.447
Bruno.

10:48.530 --> 10:49.572
Papa.

10:50.157 --> 10:51.700
I see the net needs mending…

10:51.867 --> 10:52.868
Got it.

10:55.954 --> 11:00.454
<i>Bruno's mother had a kind heart,
and chats with her warmed his soul.</i>

11:01.251 --> 11:03.419
<i>Story time with her
was special to Bruno,</i>

11:03.503 --> 11:05.129
<i>and he looked forward
to it every night.</i>

11:05.380 --> 11:07.256
Bedtime sleepy head.

11:07.549 --> 11:08.591
<i>But…</i>

11:09.468 --> 11:12.095
<i>…everything changed at
the age of seven.</i>

11:12.137 --> 11:14.430
So what are you going to do now?

11:14.640 --> 11:17.059
Well, I… I know I can't
go on like this…

11:17.559 --> 11:19.644
I have to leave.

11:20.562 --> 11:23.856
<i>After ten years of marriage,
his parents divorced</i>

11:24.399 --> 11:28.899
<i>No one would ever know why,
except his parents.</i>

11:29.947 --> 11:32.449
But what about our Bruno?

11:33.784 --> 11:36.578
<i>Mother and father
had come to a decision.</i>

11:36.620 --> 11:39.289
<i>It would be Bruno's choice.</i>

11:40.415 --> 11:44.915
Bruno, you know that Mama and Papa
love you more than anything else,

11:45.253 --> 11:47.255
but we think it's best that
we live apart from now on.

11:47.714 --> 11:49.632
So we wanted to
give you the choice…

11:49.675 --> 11:51.593
Do you want to come live with Mama

11:51.635 --> 11:53.470
or do you want to
stay here with Papa.

11:54.763 --> 11:58.808
You want to live with me
in the big city?

11:58.892 --> 12:00.977
You've always been so bright.

12:01.061 --> 12:03.146
You could finally get
a good education.

12:03.647 --> 12:06.524
There'll be other kids
your age to play with!

12:06.608 --> 12:08.818
You want to come and
live with Mama, yes?

12:08.986 --> 12:10.654
I know you'll come with Mama…

12:11.571 --> 12:12.572
I will…

12:13.365 --> 12:15.283
stay here and keep Papa company.

12:15.534 --> 12:16.535
Huh?!

12:17.119 --> 12:20.831
You don't mean…
Bruno… don't make a rash decision!

12:20.914 --> 12:22.373
You've always liked Mama best, yes?

12:23.250 --> 12:25.835
I'll be staying here with Papa.

12:25.919 --> 12:27.128
I just…

12:29.047 --> 12:30.673
<i>Mama will be all right…</i>

12:30.757 --> 12:32.800
<i>Wherever she goes,
she will be all right.</i>

12:32.843 --> 12:33.885
<i>But…</i>

12:39.182 --> 12:40.600
I guess this is goodbye.

12:42.602 --> 12:45.187
I promise I'll visit every month.

12:45.522 --> 12:46.523
Okay.

12:53.071 --> 12:55.990
<i>Bucciarati's instincts
proved correct.</i>

12:56.033 --> 12:58.368
<i>Two years after
his mother's departure,</i>

12:58.452 --> 13:00.328
<i>she remarried a Milanese man.</i>

13:00.662 --> 13:04.040
<i>He would see his mother
only at Christmas.</i>

13:04.833 --> 13:06.459
<i>But the behavior of Bruno's mother</i>

13:06.501 --> 13:08.211
<i>had a curious effect on
her former husband.</i>

13:08.295 --> 13:10.046
<i>He became possessed
with the idea of</i>

13:10.088 --> 13:12.215
<i>sending his son to a good school.</i>

13:12.466 --> 13:15.552
Papa, isn't it about time
for the customers to come?

13:16.344 --> 13:18.429
Oh, where has the time gone…?

13:18.847 --> 13:21.015
I'll go ahead and
recast the nets then, okay?

13:21.475 --> 13:23.810
Okay, then this one's all yours.

13:24.603 --> 13:27.230
<i>Bruno's father had always worked
exclusively as a fisherman,</i>

13:27.314 --> 13:30.984
<i>but now, he was working to
put his son through school,</i>

13:31.026 --> 13:32.569
<i>he needed to use his boat
to make money</i>

13:32.652 --> 13:34.779
<i>with tourists and
visiting fisherman.</i>

13:34.946 --> 13:38.991
<i>And so the wheel of destiny
steadily turned…</i>

13:39.993 --> 13:43.246
Signori, that island is
not ideal for fishing.

13:43.288 --> 13:44.914
- The other one ov—
- Whatever…

13:44.998 --> 13:47.417
We wanna go fishing over there.

13:47.501 --> 13:49.920
Just shut up and do
your frickin' job, okay?

13:50.170 --> 13:51.212
Got it?

13:53.048 --> 13:54.340
R-Right…

13:55.717 --> 13:59.846
<i>That evening, the coastguard
found Bucciarati's father,</i>

13:59.888 --> 14:02.307
<i>his body devastated
with bullet wounds.</i>

14:02.516 --> 14:03.517
He's got gunshot wounds
in the arms,

14:03.558 --> 14:04.767
- shoulders, chest, and abdomen…
- We have an operating room ready!

14:04.810 --> 14:05.685
- Seven total.
- Papa,

14:05.727 --> 14:07.186
- We have bullets still lodged in tissue.
- Papa!

14:07.229 --> 14:09.481
Papa!

14:14.069 --> 14:16.362
Please, I have to ask you to wait
until he comes out of surgery.

14:16.404 --> 14:17.571
Just try and calm down.

14:17.614 --> 14:19.866
Can you give me the numbers
of any family members?

14:20.283 --> 14:21.284
Papa…

14:25.497 --> 14:29.125
This is evidence.
Make sure forensics gets it.

14:29.209 --> 14:30.210
Si, signore.

14:30.252 --> 14:31.878
- Right then.
- Certainly.

14:31.920 --> 14:34.672
H-How did this happen?

14:35.298 --> 14:37.800
Good evening. Are you his son?

14:38.260 --> 14:40.303
We found this at the scene.

14:40.887 --> 14:42.972
It seems your father became
the accidental witness

14:43.056 --> 14:44.932
to a drug deal.

14:45.058 --> 14:47.143
He was shot to ensure
his silence.

14:47.561 --> 14:50.730
Your father is
a very important witness.

14:50.772 --> 14:54.317
We need him to stay alive
as well.

14:54.609 --> 14:57.903
- I know he'll be okay.
- So it was drugs that put my papa in…?

15:01.283 --> 15:04.995
<i>Miraculously,
Bucciarati's father lived.</i>

15:05.453 --> 15:09.748
<i>The seven bullets that tore through
his flesh missed critical organs.</i>

15:10.083 --> 15:12.251
<i>Those who happened
to have found him</i>

15:12.294 --> 15:14.254
<i>were properly equipped with
the necessary life-saving tools,</i>

15:14.296 --> 15:16.715
<i>buying him precious time until
his arrival to the hospital.</i>

15:16.798 --> 15:18.591
<i>It was the definition of a miracle.</i>

15:19.259 --> 15:23.759
<i>But for Bucciarati, the survival of
his father was a misfortune.</i>

15:26.808 --> 15:30.770
<i>Sometimes, life makes it impossible
to make the right choice.</i>

15:30.896 --> 15:34.232
<i>Life gets complicated…
We get stuck.</i>

15:38.653 --> 15:43.153
Damn fisherman have
way too much spunk, shit.

15:43.491 --> 15:45.951
I'm watchin'.
Just hurry up and do it!

15:46.036 --> 15:49.080
Damn, rompicoglioni,
making us come here at night.

15:49.164 --> 15:51.749
Hurry up and die already!

15:54.461 --> 15:56.087
Wh-Who the hell are you?

15:56.671 --> 15:59.090
Some punk kid… Hey!

15:59.549 --> 16:01.175
- What are you doing under the bed?!
- He's just a wimp…

16:01.218 --> 16:03.470
- That thing's not a toy. Drop it now!
- Take the knife away from him now!

16:10.060 --> 16:11.394
W-What are you—?

16:22.864 --> 16:24.824
I won't let them hurt you, Papa.

16:25.700 --> 16:29.078
Don't worry, all you have
to do is get better.

16:29.746 --> 16:31.372
<i>At the age of twelve,</i>

16:31.414 --> 16:33.833
<i>Bruno Bucciarati
had become a murderer…</i>

16:33.875 --> 16:37.086
<i>…and would forever be one of them.</i>

16:37.587 --> 16:39.505
<i>I can't turn back now.</i>

16:39.756 --> 16:42.258
<i>It's the endless cycle of revenge
and suppression all over again.</i>

16:42.801 --> 16:44.594
<i>I can't rely entirely
on the police either.</i>

16:45.512 --> 16:47.555
<i>The only true protector
of father and son</i>

16:47.597 --> 16:50.433
<i>would be the only organization that
wielded the true power, the famiglia.</i>

16:51.476 --> 16:53.978
<i>Bucciarati knocked on its doors,</i>

16:54.854 --> 16:58.607
<i>and in exchange for his service
and loyalty to the famiglia,</i>

16:58.650 --> 17:00.568
<i>protection was finally guaranteed.</i>

17:01.278 --> 17:05.365
<i>It was the embodiment of justice,
and for it, he gave everything.</i>

17:06.074 --> 17:08.409
<i>It wasn't long before he made
his mark in the famiglia,</i>

17:08.451 --> 17:10.703
<i>and garnered the attention
of the capo Polpo.</i>

17:11.246 --> 17:14.332
<i>Five years later, complications from
his wounds had taken their toll…</i>

17:14.416 --> 17:15.959
<i>Bucciarati's father had died</i>

17:16.459 --> 17:19.378
<i>Bucciarati despised
the alabaster apparition of greed</i>

17:19.421 --> 17:21.381
<i>that unraveled his life and that
of his very own father,</i>

17:21.423 --> 17:23.383
<i>and swore to battle it
with everything he had.</i>

17:24.092 --> 17:25.093
<i>But…</i>

17:26.428 --> 17:29.180
I-I'm sorry!
I'll leave them alone!

17:29.264 --> 17:31.015
I'll never see 'em again!

17:31.099 --> 17:32.391
That would be wise.

17:32.434 --> 17:34.936
Regret is an emotion felt only by
the living, after all.

17:35.270 --> 17:36.813
But if you're a mafioso then why—?

17:39.691 --> 17:41.067
Those are…

17:41.276 --> 17:42.860
Hey! What the hell are those?!

17:44.112 --> 17:46.239
<i>It was the moment Bucciarati
realized the boss of the famiglia,</i>

17:46.281 --> 17:48.241
<i>the man he revered
as the model of justice,</i>

17:48.283 --> 17:50.451
<i>was a leader who profited
from the drugs he so despised</i>

17:50.952 --> 17:53.204
In my city?

17:53.288 --> 17:55.498
That was the one thing
that was off-limits!

18:02.172 --> 18:03.339
And now…

18:03.798 --> 18:05.090
The boss is now…

18:05.633 --> 18:07.760
The evilness of it makes me sick…

18:08.053 --> 18:11.181
Abusing pure,
unadulterated innocence,

18:11.389 --> 18:14.475
profiting at the pain
and suffering of others!

18:14.517 --> 18:17.561
You did this to
your own flesh and blood…

18:17.771 --> 18:19.689
You're a hideous monster!

18:19.856 --> 18:21.065
You're a disgrace!

18:21.274 --> 18:25.027
You've let me down for
the last time!

18:31.701 --> 18:34.537
<i>There… Trish is still alive.</i>

18:42.212 --> 18:43.379
Good… It stuck.

18:43.963 --> 18:46.632
Cazzo, I can't get
a good look at him.

18:47.008 --> 18:50.636
I was content with uncovering
your identity,

18:50.845 --> 18:52.179
but everything's changed now.

18:52.347 --> 18:54.724
I will annihilate you here!

18:55.016 --> 18:56.017
I don't have much time.

18:56.351 --> 18:59.228
The boss still assumes
my complete loyalty.

18:59.687 --> 19:00.729
He'll die by…

19:02.232 --> 19:03.358
assassination.

19:06.319 --> 19:08.738
<i>I'll ambush him
as he tries to escape,</i>

19:08.822 --> 19:09.823
<i>and kill the bastard on the spot.</i>

19:23.128 --> 19:24.129
This…

19:24.629 --> 19:25.796
This opening…

19:26.923 --> 19:28.007
<i>Of course.</i>

19:28.216 --> 19:31.844
<i>What do churches have
beneath them but a crypt?</i>

19:32.220 --> 19:33.763
<i>He thinks that will be where
he murders Trish</i>

19:33.805 --> 19:34.889
<i>in complete anonymity</i>

19:35.056 --> 19:36.932
<i>He thinks he will
pass through the crypt</i>

19:37.016 --> 19:39.184
<i>to escape the building
on the other side.</i>

19:52.282 --> 19:54.284
<i>But here I am, waiting for him.</i>

19:58.705 --> 19:59.706
<i>There.</i>

20:19.851 --> 20:20.977
<i>He descended the stairs!</i>

20:21.603 --> 20:22.353
<i>Now!</i>

20:22.353 --> 20:26.273
It would behoove you to leave now,
Bruno Bucciarati.

20:27.317 --> 20:31.529
Step out from behind that pillar,
and you shall lose your life.

20:37.785 --> 20:40.120
Zipper Man!

20:45.293 --> 20:46.961
He's going to rip it off!

20:58.181 --> 21:00.975
Somehow… he figured it out…

21:01.059 --> 21:04.812
But he resorted to hiding again.

21:04.854 --> 21:07.439
He must have some kind of weakness.

21:07.482 --> 21:09.525
Your rationale intrigues me.

21:12.487 --> 21:14.280
What was going through
that head of yours?

21:14.572 --> 21:16.865
Your excellence and devotion
to the mission

21:16.950 --> 21:19.369
inspired in me
great respect for you.

21:19.994 --> 21:21.745
Did your newly acquired
role as capo

21:21.829 --> 21:23.205
cloud your mind with avarice?

21:23.665 --> 21:26.793
Or did your own pride and
hubris seduce you into

21:26.834 --> 21:29.628
thinking you had the power
and ability to overtake me.

21:30.505 --> 21:32.757
When Trish wakes up,

21:33.341 --> 21:36.385
I will be sure to tell her
that you never existed.

21:36.427 --> 21:37.719
Trish?

21:38.346 --> 21:40.473
What about Trish?

21:40.557 --> 21:43.476
My daughter is of
no concern to you.

21:43.518 --> 21:47.355
A demon like you could never
understand what lies in my heart!

21:51.025 --> 21:52.026
Giorno?

21:52.068 --> 21:56.197
<i>Bucciarati!
We're tracking him as we speak.</i>

21:56.239 --> 21:59.742
<i>The brooch will tell me
exactly where he is a tall times.</i>

21:59.784 --> 22:02.286
<i>Now he's at the bottom
of the stairs to the crypt.</i>

22:02.537 --> 22:03.621
<i>He's right by the pillar</i>

22:03.705 --> 22:05.581
<i>that's about two meters away
from the stairs.</i>

22:05.623 --> 22:07.166
<i>But wait, Bucciarati!</i>

22:07.500 --> 22:10.336
<i>Something is wrong!</i>

22:12.213 --> 22:13.756
You're there!

22:15.383 --> 22:18.886
Die! Zipper Man!

22:26.227 --> 22:28.938
<i>It wasn't him in
the pillar's shadow…</i>

22:29.772 --> 22:30.773
<i>It was me!</i>

22:35.194 --> 22:36.987
W-What…

22:38.323 --> 22:39.324
What's going o—?

22:39.407 --> 22:43.160
Think of this as a farewell gift
from the heart.

22:44.037 --> 22:46.205
Soon you will not exist,
so you may know now for a moment.

22:46.706 --> 22:51.043
What you witnessed,
what you just felt…

22:51.085 --> 22:53.253
was your future self.

22:54.005 --> 22:55.923
It is simply a case of
your past self

22:55.965 --> 22:57.967
seeing your future self,
give or take a few seconds.

22:58.259 --> 23:02.471
Behold the power of
Emperor Crimson.

23:02.513 --> 23:05.265
I obliterated time,
then leaped beyond it.

23:08.311 --> 23:09.812
It doesn't matter who…

23:10.313 --> 23:14.650
I shall allow no one to threaten
my eternal transcendence,

23:14.734 --> 23:15.901
never.

23:16.444 --> 23:19.155
Your time has come to fade away.

23:21.908 --> 23:25.995
Bucciarati, your mission
as protector…

23:27.288 --> 23:29.498
terminates now.

23:38.383 --> 23:41.969
EPISODE 21
THE MYSTERY OF EMPEROR CRIMSON
